Description: media playback: a stream's stereo mark handed on, and its views paired at the Stereo input filter's request
 OBS's media source decodes with FFmpeg (shared/media-playback). The mark FFmpeg reads is kept where the frames are
 decoded: the frame's AV_FRAME_DATA_STEREO3D (the frame packing arrangement SEI, H.264 D.2.26 and H.265 D.3.16, before
 the container's), the stream's AV_PKT_DATA_STEREO3D (Matroska StereoMode, RFC 9559 5.1.4.1.28.3; MP4 st3d) for frames
 that carry none, and Matroska's StereoMode stream tag for the two anaglyph values AVStereo3D has no type for. The
 media source hands it on through two procedures of its own proc handler, get_stereo3d and set_stereo3d_pairing, so
 libobs's exported API does not change.
 When the person's Stereo input filter asks, the decoder makes one side by side picture, left eye first, each view at
 its own size, of frames in turn (frame packing arrangement type 5, by the frames' current_frame_is_frame0_flag while
 they alternate, else two frames from the first; Matroska StereoMode 13 and 14) and of the two views of one time of an
 MV-HEVC stream (the stereo layer's libstereo-av, which hands on the base view alone while nothing is asked, so a
 source without the filter shows what it did). A pair is dated as its frame 0; the scaler follows the frame's size.
 A file decoded whole at its start (a stinger) is not paired and says no mark.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 61, milestone 3)
Forwarded: no, OBS asks for human-written submissions only (CONTRIBUTING.md, AI/Machine Learning Policy)
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
